// Linux x64 native backend: FFI should work when dynamic linking is enabled via `--link`.
//
// This fixture is executed on x64-linux (WSL2) by `scripts/verify_native_matrix.sh`.
//
// NOTE:
// Avoid `puts(...)` as the primary assertion because native `exit(...)` terminates via syscall
// and can bypass libc stdio flushing when stdout is redirected (as the matrix script does).

@cfg(os="linux")
@ffi.link("libc.so.6")
@ffi.ret("usize")
ffi strlen
if strlen("Hello FFI") != 9 { exit(1) }
exit(0)
